# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# MoviesApp root .gitignore
# Anything that can hold secrets, PII, or local-only state goes here.
# Per-app .gitignore files cover tooling specifics; this file is the
# last line of defence and is intentionally aggressive.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

## Sensitive files (PII, secrets, runtime state)
# SQLite databases (committed previously — see SECURITY-INCIDENT-2026-09-14.md)
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# User-secrets and appsettings overrides
appsettings.*.local.json
appsettings.*.Production.json
appsettings.Development.json
secrets.json
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
!*.pem.example

# Environment files (excluding the public .env.example)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env-azure.example

## .NET / Visual Studio
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
**/publish/
**/PublishProfiles/
*.dll
*.pdb
*.exe
*.cache
*.genruntimeconfig.cache
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.userprefs
.vs/
.idea/
*.sln.iml
TestResults/
coverage/
*.coverage
*.coveragexml

## Node / Angular
node_modules/
package-lock.json.bak
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.angular/
.sass-cache/

## IDEs and editors
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.history/

## OS-generated
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

## Logs and scratch
*.log
*.tmp
logs/
.tmp/
